Priya =E2=80=94 yes, that is expected behavior. ClaimTrack 2.0 uses the holid=
ay calendar tied to CPS-SOP-231, so the deadline clock pauses on federal holi=
days and resumes on the next business day.

For dispute deadlines, a business day is Monday through Friday, excluding fed=
eral holidays observed by the Federal Reserve Banks.

I checked a sample case from today and the system stopped the clock at postin=
g close, then resumed this morning without any manual adjustment. QA will kee=
p monitoring the first few holiday cycles to make sure the automated clock is=
 matching the procedure and the customer notice date fields are still carryin=
g forward correctly in ClaimTrack.

If anyone sees a case where the clock advanced on a holiday, send me the Clai=
mTrack case number and the transaction type so we can compare against the bus=
iness-day calculation logic in CPS-SOP-231 and the intake source in CPS-SOP-2=
01.

Thanks, =20
Ifeoma

